<HTML>
<BODY BGCOLOR="#000000" TEXT="#FFFFFF" LINK="#90FFFF" VLINK="#CCCCCC">
<FONT FACE="Arial,Helvetica">

<SCRIPT LANGUAGE="JavaScript">

<!--//

   if (document.images) {

      // Load images needed [BACK] button.

      back_on  = new Image(); back_on.src  = "../../buttons/back_on.gif";  
      back_off = new Image(); back_off.src = "../../buttons/back.gif";  
   }

   function TurnOn() {

      // Displays image and updates status bar.

      if (document.images) {
         document["back"].src = back_on.src;
         window.status = 'Go back to previous page';
      }
   }

   function TurnOff() {

      // Displays image and clears status bar.

      if (document.images) {
         document["back"].src = back_off.src;
         window.status = '';
      }
   }

//-->

</SCRIPT>

<H3><CENTER><FONT COLOR="#ffff00"><A HREF="mailto:mattstafford@x-stream.co.uk">Matt Stafford</A></FONT></CENTER></H3>

        Matt has a white 1994 3 door Tipo 16V. Matt had great
        difficulty obtaining the flexihose section of the exhaust.
        He found the only way to get this part was to get it from Fiat who
        ordered it from Italy, but only after he called Fiat UK customer
        services to complain. The part contains quite a lot of intricate
        stainless welding and cost a staggering &pound;182.68 including VAT.
        Now
        that the Tipo is no longer being produced in the UK he is very
        concerned that obtaining parts for the car is going to get worse.


